[ti:Amazing Grace]
[ar:Traditional]
[00:12.00]Amazing grace! How sweet the sound
[00:16.00]That saved a wretch like me!
[00:20.00]I once was lost, but now am found;
[00:24.00]Was blind, but now I see.
[00:29.00]'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear,
[00:33.00]And grace my fears relieved;
[00:37.00]How precious did that grace appear
[00:41.00]The hour I first believed.
[00:46.00]Through many dangers, toils and snares,
[00:50.00]I have already come;
[00:54.00]'Tis grace hath brought me safe thus far,
[00:58.00]And grace will lead me home.
[01:03.00]The Lord has promised good to me,
[01:07.00]His word my hope secures;
[01:11.00]He will my shield and portion be,
[01:15.00]As long as life endures.
